+By default, the cache file is stored in `./node_modules/.cache/prettier/.prettier-cache`. You can use `rm ./node_modules/.cache/prettier/.prettier-cache` to remove it manually.
 
 > Plugins version and implementation are not used as cache keys. We recommend that you delete the cache when updating plugins.
 
+## `--cache-location`
+
+Path to the cache file. Use this option to use a separate cache for different projects or invocations.
+
+```bash
+prettier --write --cache --cache-location .prettiercache src
+```
+
 ## `--cache-strategy`
 
 Strategy for the cache to use for detecting changed files. Can be either `metadata` or `content`.
